                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9b16110-a951-3d79-b897-f1c0b3a70b09",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An adult male of certain large mammals, such as whales, elephants, camels and seals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b96920eb-8a44-4efa-af80-65f4f856ff55",
                                                "sense_id": "e9b16110-a951-3d79-b897-f1c0b3a70b09",
                                                "text": "The quick eyes of a female caught sight of him first. With a barking guttural she called the attention of the others. Several huge bulls stood erect to get a better view of the intruder. With bared fangs and bristling necks they advanced slowly toward him, with deep-throated, ominous growls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4bb03ed-923c-4b5d-b9a1-c51ffdde2464",
                                                "sense_id": "e9b16110-a951-3d79-b897-f1c0b3a70b09",
                                                "text": "The upshot of the affair was that she accompanied me next morning. I rowed into the adjoining cove and up to the edge of the beach. There were seals all about us in the water, and the bellowing thousands on the beach compelled us to shout at each other to make ourselves heard.\n\"I know men club them,\" I said, trying to reassure myself and gazing doubtfully at a large bull, not thirty feet away, upreared on his fore-flippers and regarding me intently. \"But the question is, How do they club them?\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dcae6264-a712-3182-9a2b-8b9bdc70c658",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large, strong man."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a41c434-3da4-3ca7-987f-e134aaea82ae",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An investor who buys (commodities or securities) in anticipation of a rise in prices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08551394-2bb0-4a90-9aa9-84aff720ff49",
                                                "sense_id": "0a41c434-3da4-3ca7-987f-e134aaea82ae",
                                                "text": "This accompt has been made to appear a bull accompt, i.e. that the bulls cannot take their stock. The fact is the reverse; it is a bear accompt, but the bears, unable to deliver their stock, have conjointly banged the market, and pocketed the tickets, to defeat the rise and loss that would have ensued to them by their buying on a rising price on the accompt day […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "262563cd-308b-4034-97f3-1ebfd30cb919",
                                                "sense_id": "0a41c434-3da4-3ca7-987f-e134aaea82ae",
                                                "text": "Bulls are hoping the prosecutions draw a line under the sector's troubled past and will allow it to tap billions of dollars of cash from Wall Street."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d64aff5-00be-39b4-9008-5e589792fa13",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A policeman; a detective; a railroad security guard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f34c76af-8ed0-4180-90af-9a8b73e2b92f",
                                                "sense_id": "4d64aff5-00be-39b4-9008-5e589792fa13",
                                                "text": "You never waited until the train stopped to get off. The railroad bulls were waiting at the stops searching for freeloaders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aca046b7-8287-42fb-9388-9ba96659b2f2",
                                                "sense_id": "4d64aff5-00be-39b4-9008-5e589792fa13",
                                                "text": "The Bat—they called him the Bat.[…]. He'd never been in stir, the bulls had never mugged him, he didn't run with a mob, he played a lone hand, and fenced his stuff so that even the fence couldn't swear he knew his face."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2e07219-d54e-30b3-ab42-b7be88a5d3ff",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elderly lesbian."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c18fbe01-abd5-3947-8cc0-cc150b825197",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crown coin; its value, 5 shillings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f63c41ac-b322-4722-88b9-fae8bf1435fe",
                                                "sense_id": "c18fbe01-abd5-3947-8cc0-cc150b825197",
                                                "text": "Half-a-crown is known as an alderman, half a bull, half a tusheroon, and a madza caroon; whilst a crown piece, or five shillings, may be called either a bull, or a caroon, or a cartwheel, or a coachwheel, or a thick-un, or a tusheroon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa7ebeb8-756e-329f-b632-1ef46a6af148",
                                        "entry_id": "2788a312-2850-3faa-88c9-b0df9bc26db2",
                                        "glosses": [
